# Keep the build context small. The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so anything listed here would
# otherwise be shipped to the daemon and baked into the builder layer on every build.
#
# `target/` alone reaches double-digit gigabytes once you have built locally, and it is useless
# inside the image: the builder compiles from scratch anyway (different toolchain image, and the
# host artifacts would not be reused). Leaving it out of the context is the difference between a
# multi-gigabyte builder layer per build and a few megabytes.
target/

.git/
.github/

# Local state and scratch
*.sealed
kms-deploy.toml
docker-compose-test.yml

# Nothing under here affects the binary
docs/
test/
examples/
*.md
